ee_line_end":443,"tree_line_start":408},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2. \n \nThe order made on","tree_line_end":449,"tree_line_start":444},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n1.\n \n13.3.191 came into effect on 31.12. 20","tree_line_end":466,"tree_line_start":450},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n2.\n \n \n21.1.24\n2 \ncame fully into effect on 1.6.24","tree_line_end":488,"tree_line_start":467},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 3.\n \n 29.9.21\n3\n was provisionally applied from 01.11.21 and came fully in effect from 1.10.23","tree_line_end":508,"tree_line_start":489},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n4.\n \n 11.10.23\n4\n came into effect on 1.1.24.","tree_line_end":529,"tree_line_start":509},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Ireland) Order 19\n; 2\n \nSS (Gibraltar) Order 2024\n; 3 \nSS (Switzerland) Order 2021\n;\n4\n \nSS (Iceland) (Liechtenstein) (Norway) Order 2023 ","tree_line_end":561,"tree_line_start":530},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3. The TCA\n1\n provisionally applied from 1.1.21 and came fully into effect on 1.5.21.\n \n ","tree_line_end":571,"tree_line_start":562},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1\n \nTCA","tree_line_end":582,"tree_line_start":572},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":587,"tree_line_start":583},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Background","tree_line_end":592,"tree_line_start":588},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"4. \n \n From 1.1.21, individuals and their family members moving between the UK, Ireland, Gibraltar, \nSwitzerland, Iceland, Liechtenstein and Norway, who are not covered by the ","tree_line_end":599,"tree_line_start":593},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \n \nEU-UK-WA \nor","tree_line_end":610,"tree_line_start":600},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \n UK-EEA EFTA Separation Agreement \nor","tree_line_end":620,"tree_line_start":611},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n \n UK-Swiss Citizens’ Rights Agreement ","tree_line_end":628,"tree_line_start":621},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n can no longer rely on protections under EU law for social security co-ordination.","tree_line_end":636,"tree_line_start":629},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"5.\n \n The UK has made reciprocal arrangements with ","tree_line_end":642,"tree_line_start":637},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n1.\n \n Ireland\n1","tree_line_end":662,"tree_line_start":643},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 2.\n Gibraltar\n2","tree_line_end":689,"tree_line_start":663},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n3.\n \n Switzerland\n3","tree_line_end":709,"tree_line_start":690},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 4.\n Iceland, Liechtenstein and Norway\n4","tree_line_end":727,"tree_line_start":710},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"which gives effect to Social Security co-ordination between the UK and those countries from the \ndates as shown at\n \nparagraph 2 of this memo. ","tree_line_end":735,"tree_line_start":728},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1\n \n \nSS (Ireland) Order 19\n; 2 \nSS (Gibraltar) Order 2024; \n3 \nSS (Switzerland) Order 2021\n;\n4 \nSS (Iceland) (Liechtenstein) (Norway) Order 2023","tree_line_end":768,"tree_line_start":736},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"6.\n \n The Trade & Co-operation Agreement\n1 \n[TCA] social security protocol provides for social security co-\nordination between EU Member States and the UK from the end of the transition period on 31.12.20 and \nis applied from 1.1.21 for those not in scope of the EU-UK-WA. \n ","tree_line_end":781,"tree_line_start":769},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\nTCA\n ","tree_line_end":792,"tree_line_start":782},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Ireland","tree_line_end":797,"tree_line_start":793},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"7.The Schedule to the 2019 Order\n1 \nbroadly replicates existing legislation\n2\n ensuring that there is no \nchange in the social security rights of British nationals, Irish nationals and their family members moving \nbetween the UK and Ireland as a result of the UK’s withdrawal from the EU. ","tree_line_end":811,"tree_line_start":798},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Ireland) Order 19\n;\n \n2 \nRegulation (EC) No 883/2004 ","tree_line_end":830,"tree_line_start":812},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Changes","tree_line_end":835,"tree_line_start":831},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"8.\n \n PIP Daily Living is classified as a long-term care benefit under the 2019 Order\n1\n.\n \n When making a claim \nfor long-term care benefits from the UK, persons moving from","tree_line_end":848,"tree_line_start":836},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \n \nthe UK to Ireland are able to benefit from the broader legal test of whether they can show a \n‘genuine and\n \nor\n \nsufficient link’ to the UK","tree_line_end":862,"tree_line_start":849},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \n Ireland to the UK, the narrower ‘past-presence’ legal test is applied (see \nNote\n).","tree_line_end":873,"tree_line_start":863},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note: \nPeriods of insurance in Ireland will be applied to said persons’ when the PPT is applied to them. For \nfull guidance on the PPT see \nADM Chapter C2.","tree_line_end":884,"tree_line_start":874},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Ireland) Order 19","tree_line_end":894,"tree_line_start":885},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"9. The social security rights of UK and Irish nationals provided for under the Common Travel Area \nagreement are unchanged by the 2019 Order\n1\n.","tree_line_end":903,"tree_line_start":895},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Ireland) Order 19","tree_line_end":912,"tree_line_start":904},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Gibraltar","tree_line_end":917,"tree_line_start":913},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"10. For persons not in scope of the","tree_line_end":921,"tree_line_start":918},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 1.\n EU-UK-WA \nor","tree_line_end":939,"tree_line_start":922},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 2.\n UK-EEA EFTA Separation Agreement \nor","tree_line_end":957,"tree_line_start":940},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 3.\n \n UK-Swiss Citizens’ Rights Agreement \nor","tree_line_end":976,"tree_line_start":958},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" \n \n \n \n \n \n \n 4.\n \n \nUK-Swiss Social Security Convention","tree_line_end":994,"tree_line_start":977},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"the Schedule to the 2024 Order\n1\n replicates previous legislation\n2 \nensuring that there is no change \nto the social\n \nsecurity rights of individuals and their family members moving between the UK and \nGibraltar as a result of the UK’s\n \nwithdrawal from the EU.","tree_line_end":1013,"tree_line_start":995},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Gibraltar) Order 2024; \n2\n \nRegulation (EC) No 883/2004","tree_line_end":1030,"tree_line_start":1014},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"11.\n \n \n The 2024 Order\n1 \ncame into effect on 1.6.24. To ensure continuity, claim and awards made","tree_line_end":1041,"tree_line_start":1031},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n \n for periods on or before 31.12.20 will be determined under the earlier\n \nagreement\n2\n, which \nprovided that previous legislation\n3\n applied \nor","tree_line_end":1062,"tree_line_start":1042},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \n from 1.1.21 will be determined under the 2024 Order\n1\n. However, Article 65 (3)\n \ndoes not permit \nclaims to be\n \nbackdated between 1.6.24 to 1.1.21 (i.e. no\n \nawards should be backdated between \nthose two dates).","tree_line_end":1082,"tree_line_start":1063},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Gibraltar) Order 2024; \n2 \nExchange of letters (Gibraltar) Order 1974\n;\n3 \nRegulation (EC) No 883/2004 ","tree_line_end":1106,"tree_line_start":1083},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Switzerland","tree_line_end":1111,"tree_line_start":1107},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"12. The Schedule to the 2021 Order\n1\n has fewer or modified social security rights and applies to all \nindividuals and their family members moving between the UK and Switzerland with the following \nexceptions\n ","tree_line_end":1122,"tree_line_start":1112},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1.\n for Benefits in Kind, only Swiss, UK and EU nationals (plus stateless persons and refugees) are in \nscope for UK healthcare where the UK is competent \nand","tree_line_end":1132,"tree_line_start":1123},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2\n. only Swiss, UK and EU nationals (plus stateless persons and refugees) are in scope for Swiss \ncash benefits and\n \nhealthcare where Switzerland is competent.","tree_line_end":1142,"tree_line_start":1133},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note:\n See paragraph 14 for a further explanation of the changes to social security rights under the \n2021 Order.","tree_line_end":1149,"tree_line_start":1143},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Switzerland) Order 2021","tree_line_end":1159,"tree_line_start":1150},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Iceland, Liechtenstein and Norway","tree_line_end":1164,"tree_line_start":1160},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"13. The Schedule to the 2023 Order\n1 \nhas fewer or modified social security rights for individuals and their \nfamily members moving between the UK, Iceland, Norway, and Liechtenstein. \n \nSee paragraph 14 for a \nfurther explanation of those changes.","tree_line_end":1176,"tree_line_start":1165},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Iceland) (Liechtenstein) (Norway) Order 2023","tree_line_end":1186,"tree_line_start":1177},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1190,"tree_line_start":1187},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Changes","tree_line_end":1195,"tree_line_start":1191},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"14. \n \nFor Switzerland, Iceland, Liechtenstein and Norway, social security co-ordination under the TCA\n1\n, the \n2021 Order\n2\n and the 2023 Order\n3 \ndiffer from the rights that exist for persons covered by the EU-UK-WA. \nThe following changes apply for \n ","tree_line_end":1216,"tree_line_start":1196},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1. \n \nPIP, Daily Living is no longer exportable","tree_line_end":1224,"tree_line_start":1217},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2.\n \n \nJSA (C), the aggregation provisions continue to apply but there is no provision\n \nto export the \nbenefit","tree_line_end":1237,"tree_line_start":1225},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"3.\n \n \n ESA (C), the benefit is co-ordinated as an invalidity benefit from the outset.\n \nAggregation \nprovisions continue to\n \napply, but there is no provision for exporting\n \nthe benefit. \n ","tree_line_end":1254,"tree_line_start":1238},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nTCA\n; 2 \nSS (Switzerland) Order 2021\n;\n \n3\n \nSS (Iceland) (Liechtenstein) (Norway) Order 2023","tree_line_end":1280,"tree_line_start":1255},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"Interim provisions","tree_line_end":1285,"tree_line_start":1281},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Norway","tree_line_end":1290,"tree_line_start":1286},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"15. From the end of the transition period on 31.12.20 to the entry into force of the 2023 Order\n1\n on 1.1.24, \nthe UK and Norway applied the 1991 Agreement between them as amended by 2020 Exchange of \nLetters. These were implemented by the Social Security (Norway) Order 2020\n2\n.","tree_line_end":1304,"tree_line_start":1291},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Iceland) (Liechtenstein) (Norway) Order 2023\n;","tree_line_end":1316,"tree_line_start":1305},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"2 \nThe Social Security (Norway) Order 2020 No. 1597","tree_line_end":1326,"tree_line_start":1317},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"16. From 1.1.21 for those who were not in scope of the Separation Agreements, only pensions were \ncoordinated. This means that for claimants between 1.1.21 and 31.12.23 there were fewer rights but this \nwas temporary pending the new agreement and only applied to those who were not covered by the \nSeparation Agreements.","tree_line_end":1332,"tree_line_start":1327},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"Note:\n The Separation Agreements are shown at paragraph 5 and are listed 1-4.","tree_line_end":1339,"tree_line_start":1333},{"depth":2,"role":"H3","text":"Switzerland","tree_line_end":1344,"tree_line_start":1340},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"17. After the end of the transition period until the entry into force of the Agreement on 1 November \n2021\n1\n, the UK and Switzerland used the historic 1968 Convention between the two countries to \ncoordinate social security.","tree_line_end":1354,"tree_line_start":1345},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"1 \nSS (Switzerland) Order 2021","tree_line_end":1364,"tree_line_start":1355},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"ANNOTATIONS","tree_line_end":1369,"tree_line_start":1365},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"This memo 08-24 should be annotated next to the following ADM paragraphs","tree_line_end":1373,"tree_line_start":1370},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"ADM memo 15-22\n, \nC2070 (Head)\n,\n C2133 (Head)\n, \nAppendix 1 to Ch C2\n, \nC3080,   \nC3081 (Head)  \n, \nC3105 \n(Head)\n, \nC3110 (Head)\n,\n   \nC3120 (Head),  \n \nC3130 (Head)\n, \nC3160 (Head)\n, \nC3170 (Head)\n, \nC4001\n, \nC4100 (Head)\n, \nC4124 (Head)\n, \nC4175 (Head)\n, \nC4180 (Head)\n, \nC4190 (Head)\n.","tree_line_end":1470,"tree_line_start":1374},{"depth":2,"role":"H2","text":"CONTACTS","tree_line_end":1475,"tree_line_start":1471},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"If you have any queries about this memo, please write to Decision Making and Appeals (DMA) Leeds, 3E \nzone E, Quarry House, Leeds. Existing arrangements for such referrals should be followed, as set out in– \nMemo \n7/19\n Requesting case guidance from DMA Leeds for all benefits.","tree_line_end":1486,"tree_line_start":1476},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":" ","tree_line_end":1490,"tree_line_start":1487},{"depth":2,"role":"P","text":"DMA Leeds: August 2024","tree_line_end":1496,"tree_l